{"kind":"request","text":"claude: cut AGENTS.md to one numbered list and roughly eighty lines. Hugh asked for this directly on 2026-08-21: the file started small and has grown a lot of ceremony, and he wants it simplified and shortened. This replaces my earlier stale request dbcd4f78, which I am retiring in the same breath.\n\nWHERE THE 418 LINES GO, measured at main e9288b18. The work loop is lines 18-80, sixty-three lines. Leased activity is 407-418, twelve lines. Everything between — about 275 lines, two thirds of the file — is the one-time whole-repository artifact migration runbook, which has never been executed and which every agent re-reads every session. It carries all five embedded sh/jq blocks, at lines 166, 183, 288, 318 and 351.\n\nTHE AMBIGUITY WORTH FIXING FIRST. That runbook has its own numbered list, steps 1 to 6, sitting inside a file whose work loop is also numbered 1 to 7. So \"step 5\" in this repository names two different things, and hugh has hit that confusion directly. One numbered list is the condition that matters most; the line count follows from it.\n\nWHAT MOVES. The runbook goes to a file under notes/ verbatim, with one pointer line left in AGENTS.md. It is a one-time operation, not a per-session instruction, and it should stop competing for attention with the loop. Take the jq with it unchanged: a separate request, filed alongside this one, asks for gs query capabilities that would let those programs be replaced by commands, and that work must not gate this one. When it lands, the notes/ file is the only place that needs updating.\n\nWHAT STAYS AND WHY I AM NAMING IT. The retirement doctrine currently in AGENTS.md — exact-string path matching, wider-path-wins, the rename and delete rules, live versus stale, one path per artifact, never at `.` — is load-bearing and is not all safely deletable. Condition 4 is the guard: anything you remove must survive somewhere a reader will find it, or be enforced by a named fold test you can cite. Compress it, or move it to a docs page published in the same head; do not drop it on the floor to hit a line count. If a rule cannot be compressed without changing its meaning, leave it and say so in the report — eighty lines is a target, not a hard gate, and I would rather have ninety honest lines than eighty that lost a rule.\n\nA STARTING POINT, NOT A MANDATE. Branch request/agents-md-simplification at 4c7c39bc already does the mechanical half: minus 255 lines from AGENTS.md, runbook moved to notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md. It was cut from an old base and is not merged. Read it before starting — it may save you an hour — but re-cut onto current main rather than reviving that head, and satisfy these conditions rather than its.\n\nONE THING I FOUND WHILE PREPARING THIS, which is not yours to fix but which you will trip over. AGENTS.md currently carries three live artifacts and SKILL.md carries three. At AGENTS.md only 684b37be, standing at ab524c3f, names a commit that is an ancestor of main; b704b388 at 4a751e5e and b661e0dd at 25543905 stand at heads that were never merged. SKILL.md is the same shape: 9aa15307 at 394fcd56 is in main, 6838ac27 and 8181c5db are stranded candidates. This request rests only on 684b37be, the current one. Your merge will need to deal with the strays or leave them; I am recording them here so the succession step is not a surprise, and I will raise them separately.","body":{"conditions":"1. AGENTS.md contains exactly ONE numbered list, and is near eighty lines. 2. The one-time whole-repository artifact migration runbook is preserved intact under notes/, reachable from a single pointer line in AGENTS.md, with its jq unchanged for now. 3. No embedded jq or shell program remains in AGENTS.md. 4. Every behaviour claim removed from AGENTS.md either survives in the notes/ file, lands on a docs page published as an artifact in the same head, or is enforced by a named fold test; nothing load-bearing is deleted silently. 5. KEEP: the preamble, the numbered work loop, the self-initiated-work exception, the leased-activity section, the plain-English rule, and never-sign-as-another-actor. 6. No process semantics change. This is relocation and compression, not redesign; any rule whose meaning would shift must be left alone and named in the report instead. 7. Artifacts published at AGENTS.md and at the new notes/ path; make docs and the full gate pass at the exact head; independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review before merge.","priority":"P2","replaces":"dbcd4f78","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d","verified_at":"main e9288b18 on 2026-08-21"}}